pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Test Slack') {
            steps {
                echo 'Testing Slack notification...'
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        success {
            slackSend(
                channel: '#all-testing',
                message: 'Hello! Jenkins Slack integration is working successfully.'
            )
        }

        failure {
            slackSend(
                channel: '#all-testing',
                message: 'Jenkins Slack integration test failed.'
            )
        }
    }
}


I first create a Slack App in the Slack workspace. Then I enable a Bot User, assign the required OAuth permissions such as chat:write, 
and install the app to the workspace. This generates a Bot User OAuth Token (xoxb-...). I store this token securely in Jenkins Credentials as a Secret Text 
credential instead of hardcoding it. After that, I configure the Slack Notification Plugin in Jenkins by selecting the workspace, the stored credential, and the
 default Slack channel. Finally, I test the connection and use the slackSend step in the Jenkins pipeline to send build success or failure notifications.